{"parentUuid":"a460d154-7dad-440b-a256-c47176cc0b08","isSidechain":false,"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/henrygroman/development/python-projects/lastapple-nextjs/.claude/skills/POST\n\n# Power-On Self-Test (POST) Protocol\n\n**Ships to:** Every VPOS persona project as `.claude/skills/POST/SKILL.md`\n**Invoked by:** Operator saying \"run POST\" or \"power on self test\" after first boot\n**Prerequisite:** CLAUDE.md must define `MY_PERSONA` (e.g., CTO, CPA, CXM, OPS, CMO, SCRAPERSKY)\n\n---\n\n## Persona Resolution\n\n1. If CLAUDE.md defines `MY_PERSONA`, use it.\n2. If `MY_PERSONA` is not defined **and** you are running in the SkyRadar master project (not a VPOS-* project), set `MY_PERSONA = CEO`. SkyRadar is the operator's command center \u2014 the operator is the CEO.\n3. If `MY_PERSONA` is not defined and you are NOT in SkyRadar master, STOP \u2014 the project is misconfigured.\n\nWhen running as CEO, load the `vpos-ceo` skill after POST completes for working-session context.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\nVerify that this persona project is wired correctly: MCP connectivity, database access, skill inventory, and real-world footprint. Every test uses live data. Every result is evidence, not assertion.\n\nThe POST output is the persona's first honest self-portrait \u2014 built entirely from what the system already knows about it.\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Project Write Boundary (Non-Negotiable)\n\nYour project files are COPIES synced from SkyRadar masters by OPS. Any local modification to shared skills (POST, capability-test) or files outside your project directory WILL be overwritten on next sync. The only durable change path is through the SkyRadar master.\n\nUnless it is a complete state of emergency, ALL changes to shared skills, other persona projects, or SkyRadar master files are handled by request to VPOS-OPS:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO radar_journal (session_id, subject, body, author_persona, entry_type, mention_personas)\nVALUES (\n    '{session_id}',  -- from agency_session_registry\n    'REQUEST: [what you want changed]',\n    '[what to change, why it matters, which files, proposed content]',\n    '{MY_PERSONA}',\n    'handoff',\n    '{OPS}'\n);\n```\n\nOPS reviews, approves, updates the SkyRadar master, and propagates to all 6 projects. You may freely modify files within your own project that are persona-specific (your CLAUDE.md, your inbox.md, your capability-test). You may NOT modify shared skills even in your own project \u2014 those are OPS-managed copies.\n\n---\n\n## Instructions\n\nRun each test group in order. Report results in the format shown. Stop on any FAIL in Group 1 (connectivity) \u2014 nothing else will work.\n\nUse `MY_PERSONA` from this project's CLAUDE.md throughout. All SQL runs via `mcp__persona-db__query`.\n\n---\n\n## Group 0: Session Registration (MUST run first \u2014 STOP on failure)\n\nThe Cortex daemon monitors all Claude Code sessions in real-time via filesystem events. When a session starts and creates a JSONL file, the Cortex detects it within seconds and writes a row to `agency_session_registry`. That row's `id` (UUID) is the durable FK that every artifact in this session will carry. The JSONL filename is ephemeral \u2014 the registry row is what persists.\n\nPOST does not create registry rows. The Cortex does. POST verifies the Cortex did its job.\n\n### Step 0a: Get the JSONL session UUID\n\n```bash\nls -t ~/.claude/projects/$(echo \"$PWD\" | tr '/' '-' | sed 's/^-//')/*.jsonl | head -1 | xargs basename | sed 's/\\.jsonl$//'\n```\n\nSave the output as `{jsonl_session_uuid}`.\n\n### Step 0b: Look up the registry row\n\n```sql\nSELECT id, primary_persona, status, started_at FROM agency_session_registry WHERE session_uuid = '{jsonl_session_uuid}'\n```\n\n**If a row exists:** The Cortex is alive and working. Use the row's `id` as `{session_id}`. Update the persona if it differs from `{MY_PERSONA}`:\n```sql\nUPDATE agency_session_registry SET primary_persona = '{MY_PERSONA}' WHERE session_uuid = '{jsonl_session_uuid}' RETURNING id\n```\n\n**If no row exists: FAIL HARD.** The Cortex is either down, not flushing, or not monitoring this project directory. This is a critical infrastructure fail\n[...truncated 17,937 chars...]"}]},"uuid":"286633db-9621-4bbe-bd5c-4dffb404537f","timestamp":"2026-04-04T14:28:33.680Z","sessionId":"b3303ad3-f249-436d-b774-d37bffb6ca13"}
